From: Yuen Su <zypulsecore@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: nss: unregister an unready init context

The interface is registered before checking the NSS context state. If that
check fails, unwind through unregister so the subsystem data-path entry
cannot retain the abandoned ath11k context. Earlier failures still use the
unregistered cleanup path.

Signed-off-by: Yuen Su <zypulsecore@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -4508,7 +4508,7 @@
 
 	if (nss_cmn_get_state(nss_contex) != NSS_STATE_INITIALIZED) {
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "nss state in default init state\n");
-		goto free;
+		goto unregister;
 	}
 
 	/* The registered soc context is stored in ab, and will be used for
